<title>USA: TABLE - Cornell Q2 shr profit $0.11.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Cornell Q2 shr profit $0.11.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>CORNELL CORRECTIONS INC</p>
<p>			  (000's except per share amounts)</p>
<p>				Three Months Ended   Six Months Ended</p>
<p>					June 30,		June 30,</p>
<p>			     1997	1996	     1997     1996</p>
<p> Revenues	     $14,840    $5,884	  $28,041  $11,337</p>
<p> Operating expenses  11,759     4,900	   22,556    9,461</p>
<p>Income (loss) from</p>
<p>  operations	    1,261     (203)	    2,147    (263)</p>
<p> Net income (loss)	795     (448)	    1,295    (710)</p>
<p>Earnings (loss)</p>
<p>  per share		0.11    (0.13)	     0.18   (0.20)</p>
<p>Number of shares used</p>
<p>  to compute EPS	7,171     3,523	    7,139    3,523</p>
<p>Contracted beds in operation</p>
<p>  (end of period)     3,541     1,561	    3,541    1,561</p>
<p>Average occupancy (a)</p>
<p>			    98.0%     97.6%	    96.4%    95.8%</p>
<p>(a) Occupancy percentages are based on contracted beds in operation. Since certain facilities have design capacities that exceed contract capacities, occupancy percentages can exceed 100 percent of contracted capacity.</p>
<p>The company said improved financial results can largely be attributed to acquisitions in 1996 and 1997, new contract awards and lower interest expense.</p>
</text>
